    turnFlow: "Dealer deals 13 cards to each player and 5 to the nest (first card to dealer's left; after each of the first five rounds one card to the nest). Players bid in multiples of 5, dealer first, clockwise; each bid must be higher than the last, and a player who passes cannot bid again. When three have passed, the fourth is the high bidder. The bidder picks up the nest without showing it (18 cards), discards any five face-down to form a new nest, names trump (a color), and calls for a partner by naming a card not in hand; whoever holds that card is the bidder's partner for the hand (secret until the card is played), and the other two form the opposing team (if the bidder holds the called card, the bidder plays alone). Player to the left of the bidder leads to the first trick; players must follow the led color if able; the Rook counts as trump. Highest trump wins the trick, or if no trump was played, highest card of the led color. Winner of each trick leads next; winner of the last trick takes the five discarded nest cards. Each team totals card points from its tricks; if the bidder's team made at least the bid, each member scores the team's points; otherwise the bidder's team subtracts the bid from their score. The opposing team always scores the points they took. Game ends when a player reaches 500 or more; highest score wins.",
